== a consumer's first anchor sets the watermark
  watermark before: none
  cursor |, watermark before every entry
== a peer's changes reach B's feed, files named by B's ids
  from the baseline: cursor |<entry1> more=false
    put x.txt                  
    mkdir dir                  
    rename x.txt->dir/y.txt    <file2>
  watermark: before every entry
  from its cursor: cursor |<entry1> more=false
  watermark: <entry1>
== a rebuild keeps anchors valid
  from the cursor after a rebuild: cursor |<entry1> more=false
== a new generation makes every anchor stale
  watermark: none
  from the old cursor: stale
  new cursor <gen3>|<entry1>
== retention: an old shard is kept while the watermark names it
  pruned with the watermark on it: 0, dropped: false
== a watermark idle past its age holds nothing
  pruned: 1, dropped: true
  an anchor naming the dropped entry: stale
  an empty anchor once a shard was dropped: stale
